    "problem_statement": "SVG circle drawer coordinates swapped causing rendering issues\n\n#### Description\n\nWhen using the SVG circle drawer with QR codes, the circles appear to be positioned incorrectly. The x and y coordinates seem to be swapped, causing the circular modules to render in the wrong positions.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport qrcode\nfrom qrcode.image.styledpil import StyledPilImage\nfrom qrcode.image.styles.moduledrawers import CircleModuleDrawer\n\nqr = qrcode.QRCode()\nqr.add_data('test data')\nqr.make()\n\n# Generate SVG with circle drawer\nimg = qr.make_image(image_factory=qrcode.image.svg.SvgPathImage, \n                   module_drawer=CircleModuleDrawer())\n```\n\nThe resulting SVG has circles positioned incorrectly - they appear rotated/mirrored compared to where they should be based on the QR code pattern."
